# Code Conventions

## Existing Patterns

- Follow the surrounding module's style instead of forcing global rewrites.
- Existing code uses a mix of function components, default exports, named exports, and one major class component (`packages/excalidraw/components/App.tsx`).
- Match nearby test placement: some areas colocate tests, others use centralized `packages/excalidraw/tests` or `excalidraw-app/tests`.

## TypeScript

- Strict mode — no `any`, no `@ts-ignore`
- Import types: `import type { X } from "..."`
- Prefer `type` for simple aliases, but keep `interface` where it matches local patterns or React props/state conventions.

## Files

- Use PascalCase for UI component files.
- Keep helper and support modules in the local style, for example `common.ts`, `types.ts`, `utils.ts`, `keyboardNavHandlers.ts`, or `index.tsx`.
